//@version=6
// Scenario C: does strategy.eventrades count a trade that closes at exactly
// breakeven?
//
// The liveness scenarios never produce one -- a breakeven needs profit to land on
// exactly 0.0, which a percentage commission makes unreachable, and which an SMA
// crossover only reaches if an entry and its exit happen to fill at the very same
// price. That leaves eventrades reading 0 in both, indistinguishable from a member
// that does not work at all.
//
// This probe removes the doubt by constructing the condition: run it over a flat
// price series with no commission, so the entry and the close both fill at 100.0
// and the trade's profit is exactly zero.
strategy("Breakeven trade", initial_capital = 100000,
         default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1)

if bar_index == 2
    strategy.entry("BE", strategy.long, comment = "be")
if bar_index == 6
    strategy.close("BE", comment = "be_out")

plot(strategy.eventrades, "eventrades")
plot(strategy.wintrades, "wintrades")
plot(strategy.losstrades, "losstrades")
plot(strategy.closedtrades, "closedtrades")
plot(strategy.closedtrades > 0 ? strategy.closedtrades.profit(0) : 0.0, "profit")
